    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nCython 3.3.0 crashes compiling `sorted()` over an `or`-expression whose left side is an attribute (or method call) — `sorted(x.attr or [])`. `_handle_simple_function_sorted` dereferences `arg.type.is_pylist_type` while `arg.type` is `None`:\n\n```\nFile \"Cython/Compiler/Optimize.py\", line 2039, in _handle_simple_function_sorted\n    if arg.result_in_temp() and (arg.type is PyrexTypes.py_object_type or arg.type.is_pylist_type)\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'is_pylist_type'\n```\n\nRegression: **3.2.9 and 3.1.4 compile the same code fine.**\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\nTwo lines, pure Python mode:\n\n```python\ndef f(route):\n    return \",\".join(sorted(route.methods or []))\n```\n\n```\n$ cythonize -3 t.py\nt.py:2:26: Compiler crash in EarlyReplaceBuiltinCalls\n```\n\nAlso crashes with the argument spelled as a method call, and inside `async def`:\n\n```python\nasync def g(current_user: dict):\n    return sorted(current_user.get(\"perm_roles\") or [])\n```\n\n(The `sorted(<py_object> or <empty-literal>)` idiom is common in real code — we hit five separate occurrences across one codebase when trying 3.3.0.)\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nCompiles (as on ≤3.2.9); presumably the optimizer should treat a `None` type as \"unknown\" and skip the list fast path.\n\n### OS\n\nLinux (Debian 13, docker `python:3.14-slim`)\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14.7\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0 (crash) — 3.2.9, 3.1.4 OK\n\n### Additional context\n\nFull crash traceback (node stack + frames) available on request; the failing condition is visible at `Optimize.py:2039` — the second operand of the `or` is evaluated on `arg.type` which is `None` for this node at `EarlyReplaceBuiltinCalls` time.",
